Here’s a real fintech-grade Saga Pattern implementation for a banking money transfer system:

💸 Flow: Debit Account A → Credit Account B → If failure → Rollback (refund A)

We’ll model this using an event-driven Saga with Apache Kafka + idempotency + DLQ + Outbox — exactly how production systems are built.

🟣 🔹 System Overview
Services:

Transfer Service (Orchestrator)

Debit Service

Credit Service

🔹 📦 Event Flow
TransferRequested
    ↓
DebitAccount
    ↓
DebitSuccess / DebitFailed
    ↓
CreditAccount
    ↓
CreditSuccess / CreditFailed
    ↓
Rollback (if needed)
🟢 Step 1: Transfer Request (Start Saga)
{
  "transaction_id": "TXN123",
  "from_account": "A",
  "to_account": "B",
  "amount": 1000,
  "status": "STARTED"
}

👉 Published to Kafka topic: transfer.requested

🟡 Step 2: Debit Service
Logic:
public void handleDebit(TransferEvent event) {

    if (alreadyProcessed(event.getTransactionId())) return; // idempotency

    Account acc = accountRepo.find(event.getFromAccount());

    if (acc.getBalance() < event.getAmount()) {
        publish("debit.failed", event);
        return;
    }

    acc.debit(event.getAmount());
    accountRepo.save(acc);

    publish("debit.success", event);
}
🟢 Step 3: Credit Service
public void handleCredit(TransferEvent event) {

    if (alreadyProcessed(event.getTransactionId())) return;

    Account acc = accountRepo.find(event.getToAccount());

    acc.credit(event.getAmount());
    accountRepo.save(acc);

    publish("credit.success", event);
}
🔴 Step 4: Failure Scenario (Critical)
❌ Case: Credit Fails

Debit already done

Credit fails due to DB error

👉 System must rollback debit

🔁 Step 5: Compensation (Rollback)
Refund Logic:
public void handleCreditFailure(TransferEvent event) {

    Account acc = accountRepo.find(event.getFromAccount());

    acc.credit(event.getAmount()); // refund
    accountRepo.save(acc);

    publish("transfer.failed", event);
}
🔹 🔄 Event Flow with Failure
TransferRequested
    ↓
DebitSuccess
    ↓
CreditFailed ❌
    ↓
Refund (Compensation)
    ↓
TransferFailed
🔹 🧠 Idempotency (CRITICAL)

Every service must ensure:

if (processed(transaction_id)) return;

Use:

Dedup table

OR unique constraint on transaction_id

🔹 🟢 Outbox Pattern (No Data Loss)

Each service:

Writes DB change

Writes event to outbox table

Background publisher sends to Kafka

👉 Guarantees:

No lost events

Perfect audit trail

🔹 🔴 Retry + DLQ

Temporary failure → retry

Permanent failure → DLQ

Topics:

transfer.main
transfer.retry
transfer.dlq
🔹 🟣 Orchestrator (Optional but recommended)

Instead of pure choreography, use a central orchestrator:

Example:
if (event == DEBIT_SUCCESS) {
    send("credit.request");
}

if (event == CREDIT_FAILED) {
    send("rollback.debit");
}

